# 2. CORE PRODUCT DECISION

The project is moving toward a **Universal Connected Study Workspace**.

The student should not have to finish one study page, navigate to another module, search for the same anatomical structure again, and manually rebuild their learning context.

Instead:

> When a student studies any topic, Anatomy 360 should automatically assemble the relevant anatomy, persistent 3D visualization, explanations, relationships, physiology, assessments, clinical correlations, visual resources, and further study links around that topic.

The workspace must be context-aware, not merely a page containing many unrelated feature buttons.

The central experience should support:

- Studying a curriculum chapter.
- Studying an individual topic.
- Studying a specific anatomical structure.
- Studying a concept from an MCQ.
- Studying a relationship between structures.
- Studying a physiology mechanism.
- Studying a clinical case.
- Studying histology or radiology.
- Studying from a search result.
- Studying from a bookmarked or weak concept.

All these entry points should resolve to a shared study context.

